 "about": "A friction hitch made with a loop of cord: the loop is wrapped doubled three or four times round the rope, working up it, and its lower bight is passed through the upper bight and loaded. It grips when the bight is pulled down the rope and slides up when the load is off. Shown loose, from the front: up the rope is to the left, the load pulls to the right, and the loop's two ends, joined in the real sling, are at the top right.",
